{
 "id": "scholars-mate-defence",
 "name": "Stopping the early queen attack",
 "kind": "opening",
 "track": "openings",
 "level": "beginner",
 "goal": "As Black, you can stop Scholar's Mate and other early queen attacks, and gain time by developing while you attack the queen.",
 "priorKnowledge": [
  "opening-principles",
  "threats"
 ],
 "side": "black",
 "eco": "C20",
 "puzzleTags": [
  "Kings_Pawn_Game_Wayward_Queen_Attack",
  "Kings_Pawn_Game_Napoleon_Attack"
 ],
 "puzzleThemes": [],
 "intro": {
  "text": "Some players hunt for a very quick win by bringing the queen out early, for example with 2.Qh5, the queen to h5. Together with a bishop on c4 it can aim at the pawn on f7, which at the start is guarded by your king alone, and if nothing stops them, Qxf7 is checkmate. That is Scholar's Mate. You beat it with one habit: each time the queen moves, ask what it attacks now and cover that, then bring out your pieces with moves that hit the queen, so White keeps losing time moving it."
 },
 "parts": [
